# go-style (Kron)

Mirror of `.cursor/skills/go-style/SKILL.md`. Auto-loads when a `.go` file is open.

## Hard rules (non-negotiable)

- No `any` / `interface{}` in function signatures — use generics or concrete types. Allowed only for `encoding/json` interop with a `// why` comment.
- No bare type assertion `x.(T)` — must use `v, ok := x.(T)`.
- No `reflect` without a `// why: <specific reason>` comment.
- No `time.Sleep` in production code — use channels or `sync.WaitGroup`.
- No `==` / `!=` for errors — use `errors.Is` / `errors.As`.
- No `_ = err` unless the function is documented safely ignorable.

## Error handling

Always wrap at the point of origin:

```go
data, err := os.ReadFile(path)
if err != nil {
    return nil, fmt.Errorf("reading task file %s: %w", path, err)
}
```

Use `errors.Is` / `errors.As` — never `==`.

## Project layout

- `cmd/kron/main.go` = thin wiring only.
- Business logic in `internal/model/`, `internal/store/`, `internal/parser/`, and access-layer subcommands (`cmd/kron/<sub>/` like `cmd/kron/cli`, `cmd/kron/serve-mcp`).
- `internal/` MUST NOT import any package under `cmd/kron/`.
- Access-layer subcommands under `cmd/kron/<sub>/` MUST NOT import each other.
- No circular imports between `internal/*` packages.

## Naming

- Package: lowercase, one word (`store`, `model`).
- Acronyms: all caps (`HTTPClient`, `ParseJSON`).
- No `I` prefix on interfaces.

## Formatting

Run `gofmt -w .` and `go vet ./...` before every commit.

## Commit format

`<scope>: <imperative summary>` — body explains *why*.

## Things needing a `// why` comment

reflect, `//go:generate`, `// nolint:`, `time.Sleep`, global mutable state, `init()` that sets env vars.
